 "run": "qwen35_9b_x52_z1p",
 "dan": "\"CPU check first (verification): Z1-P on the 9B without the 60 passages where the bridge's true value stands in the lookup's passage as another entity's value: rule verbatim on the remaining 140; report beside the full-set number in the Z1 card, both ways.\" (Dan 12:50, batch53.yaml docs_1250 item 0)",
 "rule": "Per model: gap >= 0.3 and lookup extra loss <= 0.10 -> \"the split holds on his passages\"; lookup >= 0.20 -> \"the lookup follows the lens here\"; else in between. Order split (after the gate, before the data): items where the bridge's fact sentence comes before the pointer sentence vs after. \"The order pattern replicates\" if the lookup's switch under the whole change is >= 2x higher fact-first than fact-after (both CIs), as in our 65-89 % vs 9-19 %. Hard-read stratum (v3 flag): the gap within hard-read items within 0.15 of the easy items -> \"not a lookup-difficulty effect\".",
 "as_computed": "Extra loss = X0's excess = Jdep - Rdep = (S_no_jpp_rand - S_no_jpp) / S_whole per reader over the chosen passages (J++: signed OMP, k = 25); switch = the top token is the first token of the other entity's answer; gap = the M reader's extra loss minus the K reader's on the same cluster-bootstrap draws (over the original bridge entity, 10,000 resamples, seed 0, 95% intervals). Point estimates decide (EPS 1e-9); an undefined extra loss (no switch under the whole change) holds no clause (\"can't tell\"). X0's validity bar (S_whole >= 0.30 and >= 30 switches) per reader beside, not in the rule. Muse: the rule at L26 and at L36, both reported. Z1 order: the K reader's whole-change switch share, fact-first vs fact-after by the original bridge's fact sentence (K passage) against the pointer sentence; replicates iff fact-first >= 2 x fact-after (point estimates; each stratum's interval beside, and whether they separate). Hard-read: no flag in v2, so not tested.",
